{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "דגל מחנה אפרים", :translit "degel machaneh efrayim", :gloss "banner of the camp of Ephraim"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Verse begins and ends with the letter dalet, signifying the four places Ephraim precedes Manasseh"}], :frame {:text "Jacob crossed his hands to place his right hand on the younger Ephraim and his left on the elder Manasseh, insisting despite Joseph's objection that Ephraim's descendants would be greater (Genesis 48:13–14, 48:17–19). Ephraim's priority over Manasseh was then reflected in the wilderness encampment: Ephraim led the western camp (Numbers 2:18), Ephraim's prince was listed before Manasseh's (Numbers 7:48, 7:54), Ephraim's tribe was counted before Manasseh's (Numbers 1:32–35), and Ephraim brought his offering before Manasseh (Numbers 7:48, 7:54).", :sources ["Genesis 48:13-14" "Genesis 48:17-19" "Numbers 2:18" "Numbers 1:32-35" "Numbers 7:48" "Numbers 7:54"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Verse begins and ends with the letter dalet, signifying the four places Ephraim precedes Manasseh", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:26:47.268012874Z", :model "glm-5.2"}